WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.336
-With less than a week
until the election,

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.005
the president is whining
that the media

00:00:05.005 --> 00:00:07.239
spends too much time
covering COVID,

00:00:07.239 --> 00:00:08.608
and signaling his intent

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:11.010
to steal the election
through the Supreme Court.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.045
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.045 --> 00:00:17.250
♪♪

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.752
At some point, it's hard
to find new ways to describe

00:00:19.752 --> 00:00:21.187
how awful Donald Trump is.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.056
If you bought stock
in thesaurus.com four years ago,

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:26.125
congrats on becoming
a millionaire.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.226
I mean, what else
is there to say?

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.228
He's just a vicious, monstrous,

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.664
deeply repellent figure
who's willing to hurt anyone

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.065
and do anything
to cling to power.

00:00:33.065 --> 00:00:35.334
For example, yesterday,
he was in Michigan,

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.103
where he's repeatedly
incited threats

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:38.471
against the governor,
Gretchen Whitmer.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:41.741
A few weeks ago, the FBI
broke up an alleged plot

00:00:41.741 --> 00:00:43.877
by right-wing terrorists
to kidnap Whitmer

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.878
and, on Tuesday,
Trump seemed to suggest

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:48.447
that, actually,
that might not be a problem.

00:00:48.447 --> 00:00:50.950
-Your governor, I don't think
she likes me too much.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:53.753
[ Laughter ]
-We don't like you, either!

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.622
-Hey! Hey, hey, hey.
I'm the one --

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:59.892
It was our people that helped
her out with her problem.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:02.228
I mean, we'll have to see
if it's a problem, right?

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.864
People are entitled to say
maybe it was a problem,

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.166
maybe it wasn't.
It our people --

00:01:07.166 --> 00:01:10.836
my people, our people --
that helped her out.

00:01:10.836 --> 00:01:12.972
And then, she blamed me for it.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.675
-The FBI is not your people
and, if they are your people,

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:19.913
your people sure put a lot
of your other people in jail.

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.747
It's the iron law of Trump.

00:01:21.747 --> 00:01:23.682
Anytime you think
he can't get worse,

00:01:23.682 --> 00:01:25.185
as a human being,
he finds a way.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.720
He's like the Usain Bolt
of being an ass[bleep] --

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.888
just keeps breaking
his own world records.

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:33.126
Even stands like he's leaning
over the finish line.

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.294
[ As Trump ]
I broke the tape.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.763
Are you saying you think
it maybe wasn't a problem

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:39.299
that a bunch of right-wing
terrorists planned

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.267
to stage a coup and kidnap
the governor of Michigan?

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.203
My God! Trump loses,
he's going to have to move

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.806
to a cabin in the woods
and grow a Unabomber beard.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.575
Of course, even if he did move
to a cabin in the woods,

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.644
we'd probably be able
to find him.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.412
And, by the way,
according to the authorities,

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.014
this plot wasn't
just hypothetical.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.550
Federal officials released
chilling videos

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.352
of training exercises,
and chat messages

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:02.922
where the suspects
discussed their plans.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:06.258
One of the co-defendants
wrote to his coconspirators --

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.393
and this is real...

00:02:10.863 --> 00:02:12.765
Not that it makes it
any less terrifying,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.600
but these guys
are such dip[bleep]

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.702
You couldn't even use emojis?

00:02:16.702 --> 00:02:19.238
How's everyone feel
about woman, car, bag of money?

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:21.140
They talked about a terrorist
plot to wage a coup

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:23.609
and kidnap the governor like
they were ordering takeout.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:26.145
"Well, I'm fine with kidnapping,
but Ken wants Thai."

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:27.913
Ken, we had Thai last week.

00:02:27.913 --> 00:02:29.815
"Well, what if we do Thai
and kidnapping?"

00:02:29.815 --> 00:02:31.050
Because, then, if the Thai

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:32.718
shows up first,
everyone's going to eat it

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:34.219
and no one's going to want
to do the kidnapping, Ken!

00:02:34.219 --> 00:02:35.721
We've been over this!

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.490
Trouble also keeps
falsely insisting

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.158
Michigan is still locked down,

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.327
even though
it definitely is not.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.597
He's made this lie a staple
of his rallies in the state.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:47.800
-You got to get your governor
to open up your state, okay?

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.969
You'd be doing even better,
if you had a governor

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.004
that knew what the hell
she was doing.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:53.640
You got to open up your state.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.175
Open up your state,
Madam Governor.

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:58.278
Open up your state.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.279
I mean, your governor's
a disaster.

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.948
[ Booing ]
They got to open up this --

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.983
They got to open up the state.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:07.319
Hey, Governor,
let your state open.

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:09.088
Get your states opened up.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.225
And this governor should get
her state opened up.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:15.028
She keeps everybody
locked up, like a prison.

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.862
-It's not locked down
like a prison.

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:17.997
You're there!

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.465
You're holding
a giant rally in Michigan.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.968
If they were locked down,
the last person they'd let in

00:03:21.968 --> 00:03:24.069
would be
the superspreader-in-chief.

00:03:24.069 --> 00:03:25.305
This is what Trump does.

00:03:25.305 --> 00:03:27.273
Throughout his entire
campaign and presidency,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:30.142
his political success
is dependent, in large part,

00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:34.113
on his willingness to distort
plain, observable reality.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.981
He doesn't just lie
about obscure

00:03:35.981 --> 00:03:38.150
or complicated things.
He lies about simple,

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.586
straightforward things
we can all see and hear

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:43.189
with our eyes and ears,
like a weather map.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:45.224
I mean, no one
was fooled by that.

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:47.093
We all know what Sharpie
looks like.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.362
When New Yorkers get
on the subway, no one says,

00:03:49.362 --> 00:03:51.130
"Ooh! Looks like
the cast of "Suits"

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.232
has mustaches this season."

00:03:53.232 --> 00:03:55.501
And, now, Trump is, once again,
trying to warp reality.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.404
Thirty-seven states are seeing
spikes in coronavirus cases,

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.606
which are up 39%
across the country.

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:03.209
We're seeing new records
for daily cases.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.644
Deaths are up 13%.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.079
And hospitals in hot spots
are overwhelmed,

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.748
like in El Paso,
where there's been

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:11.884
a 300% increase
in hospitalizations

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.118
since the start of October.

00:04:13.118 --> 00:04:15.654
But the president
has been insisting that,

00:04:15.654 --> 00:04:17.489
despite what you can see
with your own eyes,

00:04:17.489 --> 00:04:19.658
everything is fine
and he's been whining

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:22.695
that the media won't stop
talking about the deadly virus

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.697
killing hundreds of Americans
every day.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.532
-Here's a tweet
from the president today...

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.017
-The news, the CNN,

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.585
all they talk about -- COVID!

00:04:46.585 --> 00:04:47.920
COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.957
All Biden and his handlers
and the media want

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.626
to talk about today is
COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:55.361
You know that.
You turn on this network,

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.029
there's COVID, COVID,
COVID, COVID.

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:58.631
That's all I hear.
Turn on television.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:00.066
I hear COVID, COVID,

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:01.634
COVID, COVID, COVID,
COVID.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:04.437
COVID, COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:07.273
-Sounds like he's looking
at the White House staff photo.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.508
[ As Trump ]
COVID, COVID, COVID, jail.

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:11.276
COVID, COVID, fired.

00:05:11.276 --> 00:05:13.445
COVID, son-in-law, COVID.

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:14.646
He's jealous of a virus.

00:05:14.646 --> 00:05:16.416
He sounds like he's
complaining to his agent

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:18.217
about an actor who got
a part he wanted.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.218
[ As Trump ]
COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.886
Everyone's talking about COVID.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.688
I thought you told me
I was a lock for

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:25.290 line:0%
People's Sexiest Virus Alive.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:28.027
Trump is so mad, he's gone
full [ Laughing ] Hodor.

00:05:28.027 --> 00:05:29.529
Sounds like a character from the

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:31.631
COVID expansion pack
for "The Sims."

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.466
COVID, COVID, COVID.
COVID.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:35.401
COVID, COVID, COVID, COVID.

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:36.835
If it seems to you
like Trump is jealous

00:05:36.835 --> 00:05:37.937
of all the media coverage

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:39.271
COVID's been getting,
you're not alone.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:41.907
President Obama
mocked Trump's whining

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:43.743
at a rally in Florida
on Tuesday.

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:46.012
-This week, with everything
that's happening,

00:05:46.012 --> 00:05:47.847
you know what he brought up?

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:53.819
He was fussing about the crowd
size at the inauguration, again,

00:05:53.819 --> 00:05:56.556
saying his was bigger.

00:05:56.556 --> 00:06:03.929
Hey, who is thinking
about that right now?

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:05.565
Nobody, except him.

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:09.335
And, well, what's his
closing argument?

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:11.504
That people are
too focused on COVID.

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:13.673
He said this
at one of his rallies --

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:16.042
"COVID, COVID, COVID,"
he's complaining.

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:19.478
He's [ Clap ] jealous
of COVID's media coverage.

00:06:19.478 --> 00:06:21.581
-Best thing about Obama
on the campaign trail

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.515
is the return of stand-up Obama.

00:06:23.515 --> 00:06:25.350
[ As Obama ]
And another thing.

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.288
What's up with everyone, uh,
posting pics of banana bread

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.324
during quarantine?

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:34.660
Like the contestants
on "The Great British Bake Off."

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.196
You look more like a --
like a --

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:40.099
great British jerk-off.

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:42.869
What else?
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:44.436
What else?

00:06:44.436 --> 00:06:45.805
Now, we knew Trump
was going to be pissed

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.474
that Obama roasted him,
but, to add insult to injury,

00:06:48.474 --> 00:06:50.676
Trump's favorite TV channel,
Fox News,

00:06:50.676 --> 00:06:53.545
aired Obama's speech and Trump
was not happy about it.

00:06:53.545 --> 00:06:55.581 line:0%
[ Rotors whirring ]

00:06:57.983 --> 00:07:00.720
-I only saw he was on Fox.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:02.554
And Fox puts him on all the time

00:07:02.554 --> 00:07:05.490
and they put Sleepy Joe on
all the time.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.394
Now, Fox is very disappointing.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.962
That Fox puts on this --

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.031
This would not have happened
with Roger Ailes,

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:13.265
I can tell you that.

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:15.367
-I do love when Obama gets
under Trump's skin.

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:17.035
I got to see it
up close and personal

00:07:17.035 --> 00:07:19.071
at the Correspondents' Dinner
in 2011.

00:07:19.071 --> 00:07:20.305
They say that was the night

00:07:20.305 --> 00:07:22.841
Obama caused Trump
to run for president.

00:07:22.841 --> 00:07:25.110
Fine, it was him
and McKay Coppins.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:28.180
Those two have a lot
to answer for!

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:29.715
And just a reminder --

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:31.717
Roger Ailes
had so many credible

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.952
sexual assault allegations
against him,

00:07:33.952 --> 00:07:36.922
he had to resign from Fox News.

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:39.258
That's like getting kicked
out of the NXIVM cult

00:07:39.258 --> 00:07:41.693
for being too good
at volleyball.

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:43.396
That's the takeaway
of that doc, right?

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.231
I only watched
a couple episodes.

00:07:45.231 --> 00:07:47.332
I feel like that's the gist.

00:07:47.332 --> 00:07:48.868
Pro-volleyball.

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:50.202
Aside from everything else
that's grotesque

00:07:50.202 --> 00:07:51.971
and nauseating about Trump,
he's also just

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:54.574
an insufferable,
pants-[bleep] little baby.

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.375
He whines about everything.
I mean, honestly,

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.943
who enjoys listening to this?

00:07:57.943 --> 00:07:59.277
It's like taking
your grandfather

00:07:59.277 --> 00:08:00.613
to a fancy restaurant.

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.646
[ Gravelly voice ]
They put us near the kitchen.

00:08:01.646 --> 00:08:02.681
Can you believe this?

00:08:02.681 --> 00:08:03.749
Ask if we can move.

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:05.084
"We can move, Grandpa."

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.552
Our food isn't even cooked.

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:07.786
"That's carpaccio, Grandpa."

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:09.588
Why are there two forks?

00:08:09.588 --> 00:08:11.290
In Nam, we ate with our hands.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:12.458
Trump will accept nothing less

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:15.794
than universal praise,
validation, and victory.

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:16.962
He thinks he's entitled to it

00:08:16.962 --> 00:08:18.396
and he'll whine
until he gets it.

00:08:18.396 --> 00:08:20.733
That's why he's attacking
the integrity of the election

00:08:20.733 --> 00:08:22.067
and telegraphing that he wants

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:24.703
his new 6-3
conservative supermajority

00:08:24.703 --> 00:08:26.738
on the Supreme Court
to steal it for him.

00:08:26.738 --> 00:08:29.541
-Hopefully, the few states
remaining that want

00:08:29.541 --> 00:08:32.178
to take a lot of time
after November 3rd

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:33.846
to count ballots,
that won't be allowed

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:36.682
by the various courts
because, as you know,

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:38.684
we're in courts on that.
We just had a big

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:42.254
victory yesterday
in Wisconsin on that matter.

00:08:42.254 --> 00:08:44.156
So, hopefully,
that won't be happening.

00:08:44.156 --> 00:08:45.391
I think we're doing very well.

00:08:45.391 --> 00:08:47.527
We're going to have
an exciting night.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:49.962
It would be very,
very proper and very nice

00:08:49.962 --> 00:08:53.766
if a winner were declared
or November 3rd,

00:08:53.766 --> 00:08:56.401
instead of counting ballots
for two weeks,

00:08:56.401 --> 00:08:58.570
which is totally inappropriate,

00:08:58.570 --> 00:09:01.340
and I don't believe that
that's by our laws.

00:09:01.340 --> 00:09:04.043
-Okay, first of all, why does
it sound so threatening

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:06.178
when Trump says, "We're going
to have an exciting night"?

00:09:06.178 --> 00:09:08.914
It's like hearing Jigsaw say,
"I want to play a game."

00:09:08.914 --> 00:09:11.583
Second, ballots that get counted
after midnight on election night

00:09:11.583 --> 00:09:12.752
are still valid ballots.

00:09:12.752 --> 00:09:15.654
Nowhere in the Constitution
or in federal law

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:17.556
does it say all ballots
must be counted

00:09:17.556 --> 00:09:19.658
by 11:59 pm on November 3rd.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:21.861
Election night is just a thing

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:24.163
invented by radio
and TV channels for ratings,

00:09:24.163 --> 00:09:26.532
like May sweeps
of the Kardashian family.

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.567
I mean, none of them
are even related.

00:09:28.567 --> 00:09:30.235
Two of them are CGI.

00:09:30.235 --> 00:09:31.670
[ Laughing ]
I mean, would a real person

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.539
tweet about a birthday party
on a private island

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:34.673
in the middle of a pandemic?

00:09:34.673 --> 00:09:36.875
Oh, really?
They did?

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:37.876
But just one tweet?

00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:39.645
[ Gasp ]
A thread. Huh.

00:09:39.645 --> 00:09:41.781
Point is, Republicans pretend
to be originalists

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.650
who adhere to the strict
meaning of the Constitution,

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.785
but back when the
Constitution was written,

00:09:46.785 --> 00:09:50.022
you think they counted all
the ballots on election night?

00:09:50.022 --> 00:09:51.791
Back then, it took two weeks
to get a letter

00:09:51.791 --> 00:09:52.992
to someone in the next state

00:09:52.992 --> 00:09:55.895
and you had to ride a horse
until it died.

00:09:55.895 --> 00:09:58.063
That's why Inauguration Day
was originally in March.

00:09:58.063 --> 00:10:01.634
John Adams needed four months
just to unfurl his brow.

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:03.869
[ As Giamatti's Adams ]
I am vexed,

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:06.171
Abigail.

00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:08.474
Again, that's a pretty --
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.474 --> 00:10:11.209
pretty decent

00:10:11.209 --> 00:10:13.613
Giamatti as John Adams
impression.

00:10:16.982 --> 00:10:18.317
I'm just saying it's worth --

00:10:18.317 --> 00:10:21.253
it's worth watching
the miniseries

00:10:21.253 --> 00:10:23.922
and I think, if you do,
you'll say, "Ah!"

00:10:23.922 --> 00:10:25.957
[ Laughing ]
So the Republican Party's

00:10:25.957 --> 00:10:28.794
new position
is that any ballot received

00:10:28.794 --> 00:10:30.596
after Election Day
should not be counted,

00:10:30.596 --> 00:10:33.999
even if it was postmarked
by Election Day,

00:10:33.999 --> 00:10:35.501
which would radically alter

00:10:35.501 --> 00:10:37.669
how we've conducted elections
in this country for decades.

00:10:37.669 --> 00:10:39.671
And conservatives
on the Supreme Court

00:10:39.671 --> 00:10:41.640
are already signaling
that they're ready

00:10:41.640 --> 00:10:43.242
to go along with this
absurd new standard.

00:10:43.242 --> 00:10:46.712
The court's conservative
majority refused, on Monday,

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:49.948
to extend Wisconsin's deadline
for receiving absentee ballots

00:10:49.948 --> 00:10:51.850
to six days after the election.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:54.753
And, just as Brett Kavanaugh
wrote one of the sloppiest,

00:10:54.753 --> 00:10:56.555
most incoherent opinions
in recent memory,

00:10:56.555 --> 00:10:58.524
repeating the Trump claim
that ballots counted

00:10:58.524 --> 00:11:00.959
after Election Day are,
somehow, suspicious.

00:11:00.959 --> 00:11:02.061 line:0%
-In his written opinion,

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:03.796 line:0%
Justice Brett Kavanaugh,
a Trump appointee,

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:06.164 line:0%
said elections have
to end sometime.

00:11:06.164 --> 00:11:08.167 line:0%
"States want
to avoid the chaos..."

00:11:17.243 --> 00:11:18.310
-What are you talking about?

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:19.578
If there are more ballots
to count,

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:22.415
then that means there are
no results to flip.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:24.650
That's like ending a football
game after the third quarter

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:27.686
because fourth quarter
touchdowns would flip the score,

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:29.522
which is ridiculous,
and also impossible,

00:11:29.522 --> 00:11:30.722
if you're playing the Jets.

00:11:30.722 --> 00:11:32.391
"Ah, we did our best, fellas."

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.226
But, coach, there's still
the fourth quarter.

00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:37.563
"Yeah, I...might just head out.

00:11:37.563 --> 00:11:39.098
Beat the traffic."

00:11:39.098 --> 00:11:40.866
Kavanaugh's opinion
was also riddled

00:11:40.866 --> 00:11:42.301
with incredibly lazy errors.

00:11:42.301 --> 00:11:44.402
He favorably quoted
a legal scholar

00:11:44.402 --> 00:11:46.972
who was actually arguing
in favor

00:11:46.972 --> 00:11:49.041
of extending postmark deadlines,

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:51.209
repeatedly confused
receipt deadlines

00:11:51.209 --> 00:11:53.379
with submission deadlines,
and wrote that...

00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:00.585
Which is not true.

00:12:00.585 --> 00:12:03.522
Vermont decided to mail a ballot
to every registered voter

00:12:03.522 --> 00:12:06.625
and authorized ballot processing
30 days before the election

00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:07.826
to speed up vote counting.

00:12:07.826 --> 00:12:09.728
Oh, no, is this one
of those classic

00:12:09.728 --> 00:12:11.263
"I like beer" situations?

00:12:11.263 --> 00:12:12.798
If you want to know
what Vermont's up to,

00:12:12.798 --> 00:12:15.100
just Google it,
or sit quietly your office

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.002
and wait for Bernie Sanders
to yell about it.

00:12:17.002 --> 00:12:19.972
[ As Sanders ]
Everyone in Vermont
gets a ballot and a sticker.

00:12:19.972 --> 00:12:22.074
I don't like the sticker
because it leaves a residue

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:23.709
on my good shirt!

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:26.345
This is the GOP's con --
slow down mail service,

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:28.179
limit the number of dropboxes,

00:12:28.179 --> 00:12:30.582
then, claim ballots
that arrive later invalid.

00:12:30.582 --> 00:12:32.651
For example,
Texas Governor Greg Abbott

00:12:32.651 --> 00:12:34.119
limited drop-off locations

00:12:34.119 --> 00:12:36.154
for mail-in ballots
to one per county.

00:12:36.154 --> 00:12:38.590
Meanwhile, Republicans
in Pennsylvania blocked attempts

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:40.459
to allow counties
to start processing

00:12:40.459 --> 00:12:41.961
mail ballots
before Election Day.

00:12:41.961 --> 00:12:43.995
Basically, if Republicans
had their way,

00:12:43.995 --> 00:12:46.031
there would be exactly
one ballot dropbox

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:49.001
for the entire country,
somewhere in the Mojave Desert,

00:12:49.001 --> 00:12:51.303
and you'd only be able to use it
on odd-numbered days,

00:12:51.303 --> 00:12:53.305
between the hours
of 3:00 and 4:00 am,

00:12:53.305 --> 00:12:54.573
after crossing a bridge

00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:56.775
and answering three riddles
from Rudy Giuliani.

00:12:56.775 --> 00:12:58.510
[ As Giuliani ]
Riddle me this -- how would you

00:12:58.510 --> 00:13:00.746
get a mic off
without untucking your shirt?

00:13:00.746 --> 00:13:03.682
[ Laughter ]

00:13:03.682 --> 00:13:05.451
You know what Giuliani's
catchphrase

00:13:05.451 --> 00:13:07.052
used to be, Shoemaker?
-No, what was his --

00:13:07.052 --> 00:13:08.053
-[ Italian accent ]
My cousin!

00:13:08.053 --> 00:13:12.091
[ Laughter ]

00:13:12.091 --> 00:13:14.193
It couldn't be any clearer
that Trump and his allies

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:16.328
on the Supreme Court
are telegraphing their plan

00:13:16.328 --> 00:13:18.396
to orchestrate a sequel
to Bush v. Gore

00:13:18.396 --> 00:13:20.332
by hoping Trump is ahead
on an election night

00:13:20.332 --> 00:13:22.201
and then prematurely
declaring him the winner

00:13:22.201 --> 00:13:23.935
before all the votes
are counted.

00:13:23.935 --> 00:13:26.705
And, now, they have yet another
reliable ally in their scheme,

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:28.773
with the confirmation
of Amy Coney Barrett.

00:13:28.773 --> 00:13:30.942
Barrett is such
a loyal Trump disciple,

00:13:30.942 --> 00:13:33.445
she made the stunning decision
to appear with Trump

00:13:33.445 --> 00:13:34.546
at what was effectively

00:13:34.546 --> 00:13:37.082
a White House campaign
rally on Monday

00:13:37.082 --> 00:13:39.517
and in a subsequent
campaign-style video,

00:13:39.517 --> 00:13:41.920
just eight days before
a presidential election

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.154
she might have to rule on.

00:13:43.154 --> 00:13:45.390
Ah, yes,
the independent judiciary,

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:47.125
just how the framers
imagined it.

00:13:47.125 --> 00:13:49.294
You know how bummed John Adams
would be, to see that?

00:13:49.294 --> 00:13:50.696
He'd be walking
around the house, saying --

00:13:50.696 --> 00:13:52.364
[ As Giamatti's Adams ]
Abigail.

00:13:52.364 --> 00:13:53.832
I am perturbed, Abigail.

00:13:53.832 --> 00:13:55.901
I am...

00:13:55.901 --> 00:13:57.502
dang it, uh...

00:13:57.502 --> 00:13:59.371
Pull up thesource.com.

00:13:59.371 --> 00:14:00.906
And, if you're
a Barrett supporter,

00:14:00.906 --> 00:14:03.275
you might argue that she
can accept the nomination

00:14:03.275 --> 00:14:05.677
from a president without
endorsing his character,

00:14:05.677 --> 00:14:07.346
but once she shares
the same balcony

00:14:07.346 --> 00:14:08.780
with the Roger Ailes apologist

00:14:08.780 --> 00:14:10.448
who's still on the fence
as to whether or not

00:14:10.448 --> 00:14:12.551
a plot to kidnap a governor
is a good or bad thing,

00:14:12.551 --> 00:14:14.052
you can [bleep] right off.

00:14:14.052 --> 00:14:15.721
The plan is clear --
Trump and the GOP

00:14:15.721 --> 00:14:16.822
are doing everything they can

00:14:16.822 --> 00:14:19.024
to suppress and undermine
mail-in voting,

00:14:19.024 --> 00:14:21.059
hoping they can prematurely
declare victory

00:14:21.059 --> 00:14:23.329
on election night with the
help of the Supreme Court.

00:14:23.329 --> 00:14:24.963
There's one way
we can stand up to this,

00:14:24.963 --> 00:14:27.800
and it's by voting,
in overwhelming numbers,

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:29.534
to repudiate Trump
and his enablers.

00:14:29.534 --> 00:14:30.869
If enough of us do that,

00:14:30.869 --> 00:14:32.671
then we can have an outcome
that is both...

00:14:32.671 --> 00:14:34.673
-Very proper and very nice.

00:14:34.673 --> 00:14:36.375
-This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:14:36.375 --> 00:14:39.811
♪♪

00:14:39.811 --> 00:14:41.313
God's Love We Deliver
cooks and brings

00:14:41.313 --> 00:14:42.681
over two million meals a year

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:44.983
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS,

00:14:44.983 --> 00:14:47.218
cancer, and other
serious illnesses

00:14:47.218 --> 00:14:48.820
and they need your help,
now, more than ever.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.723
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the Donate button.

00:14:51.723 --> 00:14:54.092
Stay safe.
Wash your hands.

00:14:54.092 --> 00:14:56.095
Wear a mask.
We love you.

